Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Scanner Formation Consistency Evidence Reconciliation Plan

& [PlanIdentity] is exact
  + [plan_uuid] is 119406b7-3b70-4eff-b82b-f90ea9c35d2b
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is f761e445-9961-4a1f-9adc-f973514fd542
  + [requirements] are P3TSFR-001 through P3TSFR-010
  + [state] is planned_unsigned

& [Step01_PreserveAndAudit] is complete
  + preserve raw derived source and exact manifest
  + bind selection, prior formation, current forms, lower carrier chain, and physical gates
  + decide source revision requirement before explosion

& [Step02_DelineateAndExplode] is complete
  + separate formation, observation, acquisition, order, pure derivation, evidence, form, issuance, consumption, and truth
  + atomize ten requirements, roles, meanings, states, failures, acceptance, and traceability

& [Step03_RefineAndConstrain] is complete
  + refine all material terms and anti-inference edges
  + extract and reapply twenty-four constraints
  + stop on collision or source ambiguity

& [Step04_PruneExhaustDesign] is complete
  + prune fourteen speculative runtime and authority surfaces
  + admit seven bounded proof structures
  + run seven independent folds
  + close conceptual data identities, relations, cardinality, ownership, states, failures, and versioning

& [Step05_RegisterSupport] is required
  + create final registry, ten-requirement matrix, and formation-reconciliation build slice
  + map every requirement to source, derived authority, proof route, and nonclaim

& [Step06_Canonicalize] is required
  + write separate canonical formation revision without modifying prior formation
  + state exact current vocabulary, profiles, dual acquisition conjunction, role separation, inherited clauses, faults, and stop boundary
  + define replacement formation signature table

& [Step07_PhaseLockAndSign] is required
  + recompute every input and derived artifact hash
  + reapply C01 through C24 against canonical, registry, matrix, slice, and plan
  + issue one replacement signature explicitly superseding prior formation signature only
  + retain implementation and execution authority absent

& [Step08_VerifyAndPublish] is required
  + static checks prove source generations remain distinct and production/Cargo deltas are zero
  + recursive current evidence resolves without stale references
  + record provenance, rollback, narrative, reentry, commit, push, upstream equality, and clean tree

& [Rollback] is governance only
  + before signature remove derived SJS artifacts while preserving raw source
  + after signature invalidate replacement formation authority without altering prior or raw source
  + no runtime, persisted state, receipt, fixture, or consumer requires reversal

& [StopRules] are fail closed
  + stop on source or predecessor drift
  + stop on scanner profile or unrelated formation change
  + stop on incomplete acquisition, order, scope, or carrier lineage
  + stop on supplied Equal promoted to physical evidence
  + stop on form validity promoted to issuance
  + stop on code, dependency, API, clock, platform, filesystem, fixture, execution, issuer, consumer, or effect surface
  + stop before any implementation unless a later separately preserved M2C source completes its own SJS and signature
